<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch4-chapter-ht-1p-model-and-sim" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Statistical Inference</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter covers the idea of inference, teaches students how to set up hypotheses (in 
        general) and perform hypothesis tests for one proportion. Students will learn how to apply the model-simulate-evaluate process (used in simulation studies) to simulation-based hypothesis testing. Evaluating (making a decision) about the hypotheses will remain informal/based on visual inspection in this chapter. There will be discussion on strength of evidence and what can effect it.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <objectives>
    <ol>
    

    <li>Interpret data summaries in context.</li>

    <li>Understand the logic and process of statistical hypothesis testing.</li>

    <li>Create testable statistical hypotheses in words and in mathematical symbols.</li>

    <li>Use modeling and simulation to determine what sort of results would be expected under a specific hypothesis. </li>

    <li>Evaluate statistical hypotheses by assessing the strength of the observed evidence, and understand what factors effect the strength. </li>
  </ol>
  </objectives>


